# ── Signing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The release key is the app's identity: Android refuses to install an update
# signed by a different key, so a leaked key would let anyone push a "CVapp
# update" onto every phone that has it. It never enters the repo, in any form.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
*.p12

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "build/" and not "/build": the old pattern only caught the root one and let
# app/build/ through.
build/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
*.apk
*.aab
output-metadata.json

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
local.properties
.gradle
.kotlin
*.iml
/.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
